Vector helpers take a column name as their first argument. That argument can also be col('x'), another helper, or a row closure. Later arguments are values, so a string there is a literal. Wrap it in col() to refer to a column.
A third form, col('x')-&gt;mul(2), builds an inspectable expression. Expressions behave like the helpers in memory, and they let the same pipeline run as SQL on a database table. See Databases and expressions.

School value added
The schools data has 250 students in 12 schools, with study hours, a prior score, and a final score. A regression on all students gives each student an expected score. Averaging the residuals by school ranks schools by how far their students exceed that expectation.

Method chain (PHP 8.3+)Pipe (PHP 8.5)


// Which schools do better than their students' prior scores predict?
// Fit one regression on all students, then average each school's residuals.
$schools = DataFrame::fromCsv('schools.csv');
$fit = phplyr($schools)-&gt;lm('score ~ prior_score + study_hours');
[$b0, $b_prior, $b_hours] = $fit['coefficients'];

echo phplyr($schools)
    -&gt;mutate(expected: fn ($r) =&gt; $b0 + $b_prior * $r-&gt;prior_score + $b_hours * $r-&gt;study_hours)
    -&gt;mutate(residual: fn ($r) =&gt; $r-&gt;score - $r-&gt;expected)
    -&gt;group_by('school')
    -&gt;summarise(
        students: n(),
        avg_score: mean('score'),
        avg_residual: mean('residual'),
        share_above: fn ($g) =&gt; round(\count(array_filter($g-&gt;column('residual'), fn ($e) =&gt; $e &gt; 0)) / $g-&gt;nrow(), 2),
    )
    -&gt;mutate(rank: min_rank(desc('avg_residual')), avg_score: fn ($r) =&gt; round($r-&gt;avg_score, 1), avg_residual: fn ($r) =&gt; round($r-&gt;avg_residual, 2))
    -&gt;arrange('rank');


// Which schools do better than their students' prior scores predict?
// Fit one regression on all students, then average each school's residuals.
$schools = DataFrame::fromCsv('schools.csv');
$fit = $schools |&gt; lm('score ~ prior_score + study_hours');
[$b0, $b_prior, $b_hours] = $fit['coefficients'];

echo $schools
    |&gt; mutate(expected: fn ($r) =&gt; $b0 + $b_prior * $r-&gt;prior_score + $b_hours * $r-&gt;study_hours)
    |&gt; mutate(residual: fn ($r) =&gt; $r-&gt;score - $r-&gt;expected)
    |&gt; group_by('school')
    |&gt; summarise(
        students: n(),
        avg_score: mean('score'),
        avg_residual: mean('residual'),
        share_above: fn ($g) =&gt; round(\count(array_filter($g-&gt;column('residual'), fn ($e) =&gt; $e &gt; 0)) / $g-&gt;nrow(), 2),
    )
    |&gt; mutate(rank: min_rank(desc('avg_residual')), avg_score: fn ($r) =&gt; round($r-&gt;avg_score, 1), avg_residual: fn ($r) =&gt; round($r-&gt;avg_residual, 2))
    |&gt; arrange('rank');



